{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on LP-1 step 1 (note head 97c2514b, approval d2bc38f7). Counter is the first adopter, on a fresh screen and a fresh installation in the lending room, as proposed.\nIntegration: the direct client path, not the MCP host bridge. A screen is a signed-in browser client, and it must not depend on MCP_ENABLED or on S10. The cost you name, a second copy of the B4 lease lifecycle, is removed by structure:\n1. Move the presence lifecycle (enter on mount with focus, renew inside the lease, leave on teardown and page hide, re-enter after a generation change) out of packages/mcp/browser into one module of the client package. It takes two functions, read and act. The MCP card passes view_read and view_live_act; the Counter screen passes the LV4 client live read and live act under its own session. One lifecycle, two callers, and the B4 witnesses keep passing on the moved code.\n2. The Counter screen reads the roster through the LV3 watch, not by polling. The scheduled traffic is then one renew act per refresh and no scheduled read. Use a 60 second lease and a 20 second refresh unless the binding validator refuses it: 180 acts per open view per hour, 900 for five views. State the measured Worker requests in the witness.\n3. Authority is unchanged: the screen holds no action arguments beyond the focus, and the scope judges each act under the member's grant.\nRevise the note before it lands, in the same head: this ruling in place of the open question; the checker's five non-blocking points (renew sets the deadline to commit time plus the lease; retained left cards and what happens at the budget; a restart of the child while a view is open; the DO rate read in the witness; the measure behind \"smallest\"); and a Status line that says ruled, not built. Then file the review again with --replace.\nBuild order after the note lands: LP-2 the shared lifecycle module, LP-3 Counter's live child, view and screen in the open 0.8.0, LP-4 release, install and the two-member hosted witness. I file those three requests when the note lands. They follow E2 and E3.\nSecurity gate (2efd662f): third failure, now a 5,000 ms deadline in the CLI new/check witness. Before the rerun, state what else ran on the machine during those 485 seconds (focused runs, typechecks, a review). No test, compile or pack runs beside a gate; then rerun once.\nRate after the S6 deploy, 01:12Z to 01:18Z: grow 32 per minute, lending 0, demo 0. The S6 deploy is closed.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}